==Classification==
Nyulnyul is very closely related to and was possibly [[mutual intelligibility|mutually intelligible]] with [[Bardi language|Bardi]], [[Jawi language|Jawi]], [[Jabirrjabirr language|Jabirrjabirr]] and [[Nimanburru language|Nimanburru]]. These are all members of the Western Nyulnyulan subgroup of [[Nyulnyulan]], a [[non-Pama-Nyungan]] family of northern Australia. It is possible that [[Ngumbarl language|Ngumbarl]] also belongs to this group, although Bowern makes arguments from the Daisy Bates/[[Billingee]] records that Ngumbarl is an Eastern Nyulnyulan language.<ref>Bowern, C. 2010. [https://journals.linguisticsociety.org/proceedings/index.php/ExtendedAbs/article/view/528 Two Missing Pieces in a Nyulnyulan Jigsaw Puzzle]. "Linguistic Society of America Extended Abstracts".</ref> Speakers consider these all to be distinct.

==Grammar==
Nyulnyul is a morphologically complex language with both prefixing and suffixing.<ref name=nyulnyul>{{cite book |last1=McGregor |first1=William B. |title=The Nyulnyul language of Dampier Land, Western Australia |date=2011 |publisher=Pacific Linguistics, Australian National University |location=Canberra |isbn=9780858836471 |url=https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/bitstream/1885/205021/1/632%20McGregor%20Vols%201%20%26%202.pdf |access-date=10 April 2022|author-link=William B. McGregor}}</ref>{{rp|43}} The language has an [[Ergative–absolutive alignment|ergative]] alignment system. Nouns do not have classes, but case on phrases is marked through bound postpositions. Verbs roots are inflected for person and number of its subject, tense, mood and voice through prefixes. A number of suffixes with different meanings can also optionally be used.<ref name=nyulnyul/>{{rp|44}} Verbs are also used in compound verb constructions where a non-inflecting preverb is used together with an inflected verb. The language also has a number of adverbs and particles.

Clauses can also be constructed without the use of verbs when presentative, attributive or identifying. The [[word order]] is free.<ref name=nyulnyul/>{{rp|45}}

